{"name":"Baby Cake","hex":"#87bea3","fetched":"2026-10-16","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"baby cake","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A cake with a miniature figurine of a baby baked into it, also known as a king cake."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/baby_cake"}],"entries":[{"title":"King cake","blocks":[{"text":"A king cake, also known as a three kings cake or a baby cake, is a cake associated in many countries with the Epiphany, the celebration of the Twelfth Night after Christmas. Traditionally made with brioche dough, in most cases a fève, such as a figurine representing Christ as a child, was hidden inside. After the cake is cut, whoever finds the fève in their slice wins a prize."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/thumb/4/46/KingCake.jpg/330px-KingCake.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/King_cake","wikidata":"Q177166"},{"title":"Cake","blocks":[{"text":"Cake is a baker's confectionery made by combining flour with a liquid, a fat or both, and usually with a leavening agent. Cakes are usually baked, but can be griddled. In their oldest forms, cakes were modifications of bread, but cakes now cover a wide range of preparations that can be simple or elaborate and which share features with other desserts such as pastries, meringues, custards, and pies."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/04/Pound_layer_cake.jpg/330px-Pound_layer_cake.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cake","wikidata":"Q13276"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/thumb/4/46/KingCake.jpg/500px-KingCake.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/thumb/4/46/KingCake.jpg/1280px-KingCake.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"http